url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/commits/f6f373a0b69c5c20846df37a21c1f52869fe1e04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:21:39Z","email":"oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com","name":"Oleksiy Pylypenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T17:21:39Z","email":"oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com","name":"Oleksiy Pylypenko"},"message":"Read tracking at h4 granularity with visibility accumulators\n\nSmallest read units are now spans owned by every h2/h3/h4 heading —\n''Thinking in components'' tracks on its own. Detection: each active\nsecond, every unit sufficiently in view accumulates one; leaving the\nviewport zeroes its accumulator, so read = 15 continuously visible\nactive seconds. Rails render per unit; h3 headings get the checkmark\nwhen all their units are read; chapters when all numbered sections are.\nVisual state moves to book-read-v2; stats dedupe moves to a separate\nbook-counted map so resetting progress never double-counts uniques.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RWtstNCh9hzRhTFfzGfmBW","tree":{"sha":"a636ea3b168eb0985420f5aebc3220eec263e57b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/git/trees/a636ea3b168eb0985420f5aebc3220eec263e57b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/git/commits/f6f373a0b69c5c20846df37a21c1f52869fe1e04","verification":{"payload":"tree a636ea3b168eb0985420f5aebc3220eec263e57b\nparent 524199750f0e7645e414a83a7e1b1e5748867a8e\nauthor Oleksiy Pylypenko <oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com> 1785604899 +0200\ncommitter Oleksiy Pylyp