oleksiyp/arch-book/commits/df90dca7e6598a97beaa82e7e525ea0f423b4f1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5249932?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oleksiyp","id":5249932,"login":"oleksiyp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDk5MzI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksiyp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/commits/45206c0374e7389367460e9c7642587b31ae32e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T07:03:18Z","email":"oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com","name":"Oleksiy Pylypenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T07:03:18Z","email":"oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com","name":"Oleksiy Pylypenko"},"message":"Add Chapter 13: Buy, Build, and the Economics of Dependence\n\nNew chapter after the AI chapter, making the book 15 chapters: the\ndecision space (build/adopt/buy/rent + differentiation test), Wardley\nevolution and posture lag, honest two-sided economics (with the MockK\nmaintainer''s-side view of open source), a lock-in taxonomy with escapes,\nand running the decision as ADRs with exit plans and expiry dates. The\ngateway-retirement war story moves here from the capstone''s map section,\nwhich now carries a callback. Kata: Compass.\n\nSaaS and Platform chapters renumbered 13→14, 14→15 with all anchors,\ncross-refs, figures, and exercises; Arc, TOC, chapter counts, llms.txt,\ncover.html, and og-banner.png updated to 15 chapters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RWtstNCh9hzRhTFfzGfmBW","tree":{"sha":"ab878a3cb68e3742da38dae142edc55b93ebcf47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/git/trees/ab878a3cb68e3742da38dae142edc55b93ebcf47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oleksiyp/arch-book/git/commits/45206c0374e7389367460e9c7642587b31ae32e8","verification":{"payload":"tree ab878a3cb68e3742da38dae142edc55b93ebcf47\nparent e3ff15983ab8bd70fe35cb5c4f7e8c4fc806faa4\nauthor Oleksiy Pylypenko <oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com> 1784962998 +0200\ncommitter Oleksiy Pylypenko <oleksiy.pylypenko@gmail.com> 1784962998 +0200\n\nAdd Chapter 13: Buy, Build, and the Economics of Dependence\n\nNew chapter after the AI chapter, making the book 15 chapters: the\ndecision space (build/adopt/buy/rent + differentiation test), Wardley\nevolution and posture lag, honest two-sided economics (with the MockK\nmaintainer''s-side view of open source), a lock-in taxonomy with escapes,\nand running the decision as ADRs with exit plans and expiry dates. The\ngateway-retirement war story moves here from the capstone''s map section,\nwhich now carries a callback. Kata: Compass.\n\nSaaS and Platform chapters renumbered 13→14, 14→15 with all anchors,\ncross-refs, figures, and exercises; Arc, TOC, chapter counts, llms.txt,\ncover.html, and og-banner.png updated to 15 chapters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RWtstNCh9hzRhTFfzGfmBW\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg6rSgkkt3JsnjVIJ2MehcZm+90D\nn4xvSahKxQa0CWZ70AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJ1bZOjrPiZiYY/nGtT1J/U80woXo5/Jmi+LMKg7TUJxcmFTcZZcbXwEGWla4iAFFZ\ns+Cp/JVJbr6/9vN/DYLgI=\n-----END SSH SIG