cf3ce67ae398629e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T20:23:08Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T20:23:08Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: admin section - real users/monitors management, not just Django admin\n\nSecond piece of the admin-panel epic. New adminpanel app - no models of\nits own, pure aggregation over accounts/monitors/incidents/flags, since\n\"list users with their monitor count\" and \"system stats\" both genuinely\nspan multiple apps rather than belonging to one. Named adminpanel, not\nadmin, since Django''s own built-in admin app already owns that name.\n\nAdminUserViewSet deliberately only mixes in List/Retrieve/Update - no\ncreate, no destroy. is_active is the only writable field on the\nserializer; username/email/is_staff stay read-only even if someone\ncrafts the PATCH body by hand - promoting to staff or deleting an\naccount stays a manage.py/Django-admin action, not a button in a v1\npanel. AdminStatsView is a flat summary: total users, monitors, ongoing\nincidents, feature flags.\n\nAlso added GET /api/accounts/me/ (in accounts, not adminpanel - it''s\nidentity, not admin data) so the frontend can know who''s logged in and\nwhether they''re staff without decoding the JWT itself.\n\nFrontend: AuthContext now also fetches /me/ once per login (same\nfetch-once pattern as flags) and exposes `user`. RequireStaff is a new\nroute guard - renders a loading state while user is still null rather\nthan bouncing a real staff member to /monitors for a split second before\nthe fetch resolves. AdminPage: stats tiles, a users table (deactivate/\nreactivate), a feature-flags table (create/toggle-global/delete) - same\nlist-plus-form pattern as everywhere else in this app, no new UI\nparadigm invented. An \"Admin\" link appears in MonitorsPage''s header only\nfor staff.\n\nVerified: backend - /me/ reports is_staff correctly for both kinds of\nuser, /api/admin/* 403s for non-staff and 200s for staff with correct\ndata, is_active toggle actually works and other fields stay read-only\neven when explicitly attempted, and a deactivated user''s own login\nimmediately 401s. Frontend, real browser: non-staff sees no Admin link\nand gets redirected away from /admin by URL; staff sees the link, and\nevery action on the page (create/toggle/delete a flag, deactivate a\nuser) was checked against the database afterward, not just the UI''s\noptimistic state.","tree":{"sha":"be22c6f99c935448c95711da1ad29e4c318c4dfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/be22c6f99c935448c95711da1ad29e4c318c4dfa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/68c3cab95f867b43b07004dcf3ce67ae398629e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/68c3cab95f867b43b07004dcf3ce67ae398629e9","n