0abdc0c"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5","sha":"81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5"}],"sha":"e73312fac471c8bfc6fc45d0fd37e39c5c1653ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/e73312fac471c8bfc6fc45d0fd37e39c5c1653ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:43:02Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:43:02Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: auth headers for protected monitors (encrypted credentials)\n\nCloses the gap flagged earlier - a monitor behind login just read as\n\"down\" since perform_check sent zero credentials. Added auth_type (NONE/\nBASIC/BEARER/API_KEY), auth_header_name, and an encrypted credential to\nMonitor; build_auth_kwargs() turns that config into whatever\nrequests.request(**kwargs) needs.\n\nThe real decision was how to store someone''s API key/token at rest.\nWent with symmetric encryption (Fernet, via the cryptography library) -\nnot hashing, since perform_check needs the real value back to put on the\noutgoing request, not just to compare it. Rolled it by hand (two\nfunctions, encrypt/decrypt, one key from FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY in .env)\nrather than a third-party encrypted-fields package - same reasoning as\neverywhere else here, fewer things to trust with something this\nsensitive. auth_credential is a Python property, not a real field -\nreading it decrypts on the fly, setting it encrypts - so the rest of the\ncodebase just uses it like a normal attribute.\n\nNever returned through the API, full stop - the serializer field is\nwrite_only, and has_auth_credential (a boolean) is how the frontend\nshows \"something''s configured\" without the value ever coming back, even\nto the monitor''s own owner. Mirrors how Django never returns a password.\n\nFrontend: a collapsed \"Protected endpoint?\" section on the monitor\ncreation form (collapsed by default, most monitors don''t need it), a\npassword-masked credential input, and \"BEARER (credential stored)\" on\nthe detail page instead of the value. No edit capability for this (or\nanything else on a monitor) yet - that gap already existed, not new here.\n\nVerified: encryption round-trip (ciphertext != plaintext, decrypts\ncorrectly), serializer never leaks the credential in any response, and\nall three auth types actually arrive on the wire against a real header-\nechoing test service (postman-echo.com) - correct Bearer header, correct\ncustom API-key header, correctly base64-encoded Basic auth. Verified in\na real browser too: filled in a bearer token, created the monitor,\nconfirmed the token appears nowhere in the rendered detail page.","tree":{"sha":"14d18e265a6dfa829787dc9e64d94b8d67cae8ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/14d18e265a6dfa829787dc9e64d94b8d67cae8ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5","node_id":"C_kwDOTf-iRdoAKDgxYmU1NWY4NWExNmUyNmZkN2ZhYWYxZTVjNTNmMGYxMWU4ZTNiYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/b29013bc013e5e6f8779e999f039572490abdc0c","sha":"b29013bc013e5e6f8779e999f039572490abdc0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/b29013bc013e5e6f8779e999f039572490abdc0c"}],"sha":"81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/81be55f85a16e26fd7faaf1e5c53f0f11e8e3ba5"},{"author":{"avat