i.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/e39d65b09c758e3fcdb79b56d487ffbd647d529a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:03:35Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:03:35Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: dashboard redesign - status colors, pulse/alert animations, metrics\n\nUsed Claude''s dataviz skill for this rather than picking colors by eye -\nadopted its validated default palette: fixed status colors (good/warning/\nserious/critical) that are never reused for anything else, proper light/\ndark surface + ink tokens, and the stat-tile contract for the metrics row.\n\nStatusDot is the one component every status indicator goes through now -\nmonitors table, monitor detail header, CheckHistory''s per-row status, and\nIncidentHistory (reused with upLabel=\"resolved\"/downLabel=\"ongoing\" so an\nincident''s state uses the same visual language as a monitor''s, instead of\na second ad-hoc color scheme). Every dot ships with a text label, never\ncolor alone, per the skill''s accessibility rule.\n\nTwo animations: a calm 2s outward ring for \"up\" (reads as alive, not\nurgent), a tighter 1.1s glow pulse for \"down\" (reads as needs-attention\nwithout an actual flashing strobe - kept well under WCAG''s 3Hz seizure\nthreshold). Both collapse under prefers-reduced-motion via one global\nrule rather than per-component checks.\n\nMetricsBar adds the stat-tile row (Monitors/Up/Down/Ongoing incidents)\nthe dashboard should lead with - needed monitor.current_status on the\nbackend serializer (derived from the latest Check, one extra query per\nmonitor, not prefetched - fine at this scale) so the frontend isn''t\nfiring N requests just to know who''s up. Also made listIncidents''\nmonitorId optional so the ongoing-incidents count could query across all\nmonitors instead of one at a time.\n\nAlso finally rendered the SSL data from the previous milestone (ssl_valid/\nssl_expires_at) in CheckHistory - was deliberately deferred there to avoid\nbuilding plain table columns just to restyle them immediately after.\n\nVerified in a real (headless) browser, light AND dark mode: seeded a demo\nuser with one up/one down monitor plus an ongoing incident, screenshotted\nboth color schemes, zero console errors in either. Confirmed via\ngetComputedStyle that both animations actually apply (right keyframe\nnames, right durations), not just present in the CSS unused.","tree":{"sha":"8002a710a45f82b9bd94c1029d79db2b61ef8b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/8002a710a45f82b9bd94c1029d79db2b61ef8b4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/e39d65b09c758e3fcdb79b56d487ffbd647d529a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https: