,"name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: Google login (Identity Services ID-token flow)\n\nWent with ID-token verification instead of the server-side auth-code\nexchange: frontend gets an ID token straight from Google''s own JS\n(@react-oauth/google), backend verifies it''s genuinely from Google and\nmeant for our Client ID (google-auth), then issues our own JWT pair via\nsimplejwt - same response shape as /api/auth/token/, so the frontend\ntreats a Google login identically to a password one. No redirect URI, no\nclient secret needed for this path - only the Client ID is used.\n\nBackend: POST /api/auth/google/, get_or_create''s a User by\nusername=email from the verified token, set_unusable_password() on\nfirst creation since there''s no password to log in with any other way.\n\nFrontend: GoogleLoginButton wraps @react-oauth/google''s GoogleLogin,\ndropped onto both Login and Register pages (same button either way,\nfirst login creates the account). GoogleOAuthProvider wraps the app in\nmain.jsx with the Client ID from VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID - not secret,\nmeant to end up in browser JS.\n\nVerified: backend correctly 400s a missing token and 401s a garbage one.\nFrontend build succeeds; confirmed in a real (headless) browser that\nGoogle''s actual button renders with the correct Client ID embedded in\nits request. Couldn''t verify a real successful sign-in end to end - that\nneeds an interactive Google consent screen - and hit a \"given origin not\nallowed\" console error on first check, which is Google''s authorized-\norigins setting still propagating (documented as up to a few hours), not\na bug here.","tree":{"sha":"f9d341282369c4535660a6c3190c0d129b557b05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/f9d341282369c4535660a6c3190c0d129b557b05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/83cfc9d969b731d66cf25b1990f707cf30f6f9b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"ve