s","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T18:15:23Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T18:15:23Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: incident escalation - re-notify while still down\n\nAdapted from how Sentry handles ongoing issues: don''t send one alert and\ngo quiet on something still broken. Added Incident.last_escalated_at and\nan ESCALATION_INTERVAL (15min) in incidents.services - when a check fails\nand there''s already an ongoing incident, evaluate_incident now checks how\nlong since the last notification (opened or escalated) and fires another\n''escalated'' email if that''s past the interval, instead of just no-op''ing\nlike it used to. No cap on repeat count - \"still down\" stays true for as\nlong as it''s true.\n\nalerts.tasks gets its own ''escalated'' email template rather than falling\nthrough to the resolved-email branch, so a re-notify doesn''t read like a\nduplicate of the opened email.\n\nVerified by backdating started_at/last_escalated_at in a shell test\n(waiting 15 real minutes isn''t practical to test with) run through an\nactual Celery worker - confirmed the full sequence (opened, escalated,\nescalated again after backdating a second time, resolved) all sent\nsuccessfully, and that an immediate repeat check right after opening or\nescalating correctly sends nothing - the interval gate actually gates.","tree":{"sha":"57dde9dadd30a5d2425c220526fc2fe43e593bba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/57dde9dadd30a5d2425c220526fc2fe43e593bba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/298e3d2ff2c771d144d70bb4d65c3265c14b0ca3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","