,"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/ddb6215344d39b200a5e5ed6693465fc3fc8acbe","node_id":"C_kwDOTf-iRdoAKGRkYjYyMTUzNDRkMzliMjAwYTVlNWVkNjY5MzQ2NWZjM2ZjOGFjYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/7edcd944d4157bf3bfca090d4a8c163c18f672bd","sha":"7edcd944d4157bf3bfca090d4a8c163c18f672bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/7edcd944d4157bf3bfca090d4a8c163c18f672bd"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commit/c7011af392da4c2554272f6150fc0c8305e61f4f","sha":"c7011af392da4c2554272f6150fc0c8305e61f4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/c7011af392da4c2554272f6150fc0c8305e61f4f"}],"sha":"ddb6215344d39b200a5e5ed6693465fc3fc8acbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/ddb6215344d39b200a5e5ed6693465fc3fc8acbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anjeelupreti","id":154815988,"login":"anjeelupreti","node_id":"U_kgDOCTpN9A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/c7011af392da4c2554272f6150fc0c8305e61f4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T14:59:55Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T14:59:55Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: email alerts on incident open/resolve\n\nAdded AlertChannel (where to notify) and Notification (delivery log) to\nthe alerts app. incidents.services.evaluate_incident now queues\nalerts.tasks.notify_incident via Celery whenever it opens or resolves an\nincident, same reasoning as the ping logic: sending mail can be slow, so\nit happens off the request/task path that matters, not inline.\n\nOnly email actually sends right now (Gmail SMTP, credentials in .env,\ngitignored). Slack/webhook are modeled on AlertChannel.channel_type but\nhave no sender yet - notify_incident logs a failed Notification for those\ninstead of pretending they don''t exist, so it''s visible in the delivery\nlog rather than silently doing nothing.\n\nVerified end-to-end: forced an incident open and resolve, confirmed real\nemails sent via Gmail SMTP and logged, then confirmed the same flow works\nthrough an actual Celery worker consuming the queued task, not just the\nsynchronous test path.","tree":{"sha":"eaf4cd03f74f58cf23e63803e1fbef607bc36a4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/eaf4cd03f74f58cf23e63803e1fbef607bc36a4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a