eelupreti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/commits/9456b625e08f6853f36c0bc56d366c5a1a48b5b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T09:22:50Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T09:22:50Z","email":"upretianjeel@gmail.com","name":"anjeelupreti"},"message":"feat: Celery monitoring engine + READMEs for every app\n\nEngine: monitors.tasks.dispatch_due_checks runs on a beat tick, finds\nmonitors whose interval has elapsed, and queues checks.tasks.perform_check\nper monitor. Kept the ping/detect/notify concerns split by app (checks pings\nand records, incidents decides what counts as an outage) so each piece can\nbe understood and debugged on its own. Requires 3 consecutive failures\nbefore opening an incident to avoid alerting on single blips.\n\nAdded a README to every app plus backend/deployment/frontend/root, written\nas first-person build notes rather than formal docs, so the reasoning\nbehind each decision (why Postgres in dev, why apps are split this way,\nwhy the engine works the way it does) stays attached to the code instead\nof living only in chat history.","tree":{"sha":"cf1153cd179b53e6b0bfe91b550aefd298e1b074","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/trees/cf1153cd179b53e6b0bfe91b550aefd298e1b074"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anjeelupreti/apiPulse/git/commits/9456b625e08f6853f36c0bc56d366c5a1a48b5b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154815988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anjeelupreti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id